.TH V23-INTRO 2
.SH NAME
intro, v23 \- Vanadium secure RPC and blessings for Inferno
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "keyring.m";
include "v23.m";
v23sec := load V23security V23security->PATH;
v23rpc := load V23rpc V23rpc->PATH;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is an Inferno/Limbo port of core ideas from
.I Vanadium
.RB ( https://github.com/vanadium/core ,
.BR v.io ).
Vanadium provides mutually authenticated, authorization-aware RPC based on
.I principals
(key pairs) and
.I blessings
(named certificate chains with caveats).
.PP
The Inferno modules are:
.TP
.IR v23-security (2)
Principals, blessings, caveats, blessing patterns, and ACL checks.
.TP
.IR v23-rpc (2)
Framed RPC over
.IR dial (2)
with a blessing exchange at connect time.
.PP
Commands:
.IR v23-principal (1),
.IR v23-fortune (1),
.IR v23-selftest (1),
.IR v23-fortuned (8).
Wm demo:
.IR v23fortune (1)
.RB ( Misc / Vanadium menu ).
Wire framing is described in
.IR v23 (6).
.PP
Concepts follow the Vanadium security model
(principals, blessings, caveats, patterns) but the on-the-wire encoding is
Inferno-native (length-prefixed text over
.IR msgio (2)),
not Google VOM.
Limbo↔Limbo use is intentional for this port;
interop with Go
.B v.io
clients requires a VOM (or compatible) codec.
.SS Principals and blessings
A
.B principal
is an Elgamal (via
.IR keyring-intro (2))
public/private key pair.
A
.B blessing
binds a colon-separated human-readable name to a public key as a chain of
certificates, each signed by the previous principal, optionally restricted by
.BR caveats .
Delegation is
.B Bless:
a principal extends one of its blessings with a new name component for another
public key.
.SS Patterns and authorization
Blessing
.B patterns
select names for ACLs and the blessing store.
.B ...
matches any name;
a pattern ending in
.B :$
matches only exactly;
otherwise a pattern matches itself and any extension
.RI ( alice
matches
.BR alice:friend ).
.SS RPC
.IR v23-rpc (2)
exchanges encoded blessings at handshake, verifies them against configured
roots, applies an allow-list of patterns, then runs string method/argument
calls until
.BR CLOSE .
